employer_name_irc = The Iron Ring Company
employer_name_irc_command = Iron Ring
employer_description_irc = Founded as a Shinohara subsidiary, the Iron Ring Company later became an independent salvage supplier. It operates yards and recovery crews around recurrence-active wreck fields, selling equipment to anyone able to pay and deliver salvage on schedule.

employer_name_pta = Pang Tai Arms
employer_name_pta_command = Pang Tai Navalcomm
employer_description_pta = An independent arms maker from beyond Crescent that competes through reliable, affordable infantry weapons and small-vessel systems. Its Taypani contracts use neutral brokers and Free Company routes to avoid dependence on one corporate supply chain.

employer_name_icm = Ihijerika Civilian Manufacturing
employer_name_icm_command = Ihijerika Centcomm
employer_description_icm = A Taypani producer of civilian vessels, luxury goods, and basic survival equipment. Its inexpensive, repairable hulls are common among spacers starting out or rebuilding after a costly Turning.

employer_name_ipc = Interdyne Pharmaceuticals
employer_name_ipc_command = Interdyne Command
employer_description_ipc = A core TFCF member providing trauma medicine, pharmaceuticals, cybernetics, cloning support, insurance, body recovery, and TraumaSec protection. A paid client is treated as a responsibility, though the policy terms can be predatory.

employer_name_gsc = Gorlex Security Consulting
employer_name_gsc_command = Gorlex Command
employer_description_gsc = The TFCF's principal armed contractor. Gorlex provides escorts, bounty work, interdiction, boarding, deniable raids, and contract enforcement; whether an operation is called privateering or piracy usually depends on whose paperwork is recognized.

employer_name_saw = Shipbreaker Astronautics Workers Union
employer_name_saw_command = SAW Crew Council
employer_description_saw = A worker-owned TFCF collective providing mining, salvage, shipbreaking, repair, material recovery, and improvised construction. Its crews reject both corporate bosses and automatic subordination to distant revolutionary committees.

employer_name_cdt = Cyberdawn Technologies
employer_name_cdt_command = Cyberdawn Command
employer_description_cdt = A TFCF technology and intelligence company specializing in signals, electronic warfare, intrusion, experimental weapons, recurrence calibration, precision systems, and psionic countermeasures. It promises results to the Federation without surrendering every proprietary method.

employer_name_scribes = The Imperial Charter of Scribes
employer_name_scribes_command = Saintsworn Scholastic Office
employer_description_scribes = A chartered Imperial body of researchers, archivists, navigators, and technical specialists. It preserves certified baselines and records, then adapts advanced systems to the phase conditions of the current Taypani cycle.

# Legacy employer IDs retained for character compatibility; canonical noble houses remain player-created space.
employer_name_osteen = Chartered Burgher Consortium
employer_name_osteen_command = Olywier Charter Commerce Office
employer_description_osteen = A consortium of lenders, guild masters, warehouse operators, and freight brokers recognized under Count Olywier's charter. It finances extraction and military supply while defending burgher contracts against arbitrary requisition.

employer_name_vogsburg = Olywier Charter Household
employer_name_vogsburg_command = Edelheim Court
employer_description_vogsburg = The administrative and household service surrounding Count Olywier Rabenau's Crescent charter. It supports the court, archives, subordinate privileges, military obligations, and political bargains that turn the Count's seal into practical government.

employer_name_imperialnavy = Imperial Charter Garrison
employer_name_imperialnavy_command = Lord Admiral's Command
employer_description_imperialnavy = The military arm of Count Olywier's regional charter, combining household personnel, noble retainers, chartered auxiliaries, hired specialists, Saintsworn personnel, and locally raised troops under the Lord Admiral's operational command.

employer_name_homeguard = Union Homeguard
employer_name_homeguard_command = League Naval Command
employer_description_homeguard = The professional Crescent military descended from local cadres trained by Workers' Union officers during the first uprising. The Homeguard is a Crescent force using Union doctrine, not an imported army.

employer_name_vrachev = Alyans Vrachev
employer_name_vrachev_command = League Medical Command
employer_description_vrachev = A revolutionary medical and research organization that treats workers, supports Homeguard operations, and performs the current-cycle calibration needed to keep advanced Taypani medicine functioning.

employer_name_sindikat = Sindikat Inzenjera
employer_name_sindikat_command = League Industrial Command
employer_description_sindikat = An engineering labor organization responsible for construction, repair, munitions, vessels, and maintenance of critical League infrastructure under worker, Union, or wartime administration.

employer_name_logistics = Taypani Logistics Union
employer_name_logistics_command = League Logistics Command
employer_description_logistics = The NCWL's freight and allocation network, moving fuel, ammunition, salvage, industrial material, and civilian necessities between the active front, neutral markets, and the secure rear in Chengridz.

humanoid-profile-editor-employer-label = Employer

character-employer-requirement = You must{$inverted ->
    [true]{" "}not
    *[other]{""}
} be employed by one of these: {$employers}

employer_name_nanotrasen = Shinohara Heavy Industries
employer_name_nanotrasen_command = Shinohara Highcomm
employer_description_nanotrasen = The economic engine of the Known Cluster and the galaxy’s foremost leader in phoron research. With near-total control over the galactic economy and infrastructure, Shinohara presents itself as a champion of progress and prosperity—though critics argue it values profit above all else.

employer_name_unemployed = Unemployed
employer_description_unemployed = Whether down on their luck or simply unwilling to work, the unemployed survive however they can. Some live off government subsidies, others turn to freelance work—or less legal alternatives. Either way, society tends to look down on them.

employer_name_hephaestusindustries = Hephaestus Industries
employer_name_hephaestusindustries_command = Hephaestus Industries Command
employer_description_hephaestusindustries = A sprawling manufacturing conglomerate responsible for producing everything from mining drills to military hardware. If it has moving parts, Hephaestus probably made it. Known for their no-nonsense corporate culture and deep ties to industrial and frontier colonies.

employer_name_einsteinengines = Einstein Engines
employer_name_einsteinengines_command = Einstein Engines Command
employer_description_einsteinengines = The galaxy’s premier manufacturer of FTL drives and starship technology. Despite their technical prowess, the company is infamous for harsh working conditions, cutthroat internal politics, and an aggressive legal department that makes their lawsuits as feared as their patents.

employer_name_zenghupharmaceuticals = Zeng-Hu Pharmaceuticals
employer_name_zenghupharmaceuticals_command = Zeng-Hu Pharmaceuticals Command
employer_description_zenghupharmaceuticals = The leading name in biotechnology, cybernetics, and pharmaceuticals. Their cutting-edge medical treatments and cybernetic implants have saved countless lives, but their ethics are often called into question—especially by those who can't afford their exorbitant prices.

employer_name_zavodskoiinterstellar = Zavodskoi Interstellar
employer_name_zavodskoiinterstellar_command = Zavodskoi Interstellar Command
employer_description_zavodskoiinterstellar = Zavodskoi Interstellar, formerly Necropolis Industries, is a weapons and aerospace manufacturing and development conglomerate. Zavodskoi distributes everything from light to heavy arms, space vessel weapons, ship-building, aircraft, ground vehicles, combat spacesuits, and military software. They also produce the Z.I. line of positronics, used for private security and military contracting.

employer_name_interdyne = Interdyne
employer_name_interdyne_command = Interdyne Command
employer_description_interdyne = A leading name in Solarian biomedical research, cybernetics, and pharmaceutical development. Unlike its competitor Zeng-Hu, Interdyne takes a more pragmatic approach, prioritising efficiency and durability over elegance. Its advanced medical implants and combat-grade augmentations are standard issue in the Solarian military, making it the go-to choice for those who expect to take a beating—and keep fighting.

employer_name_idrisincorporated = Idris Incorporated
employer_name_idrisincorporated_command = Idris Incorporated Command
employer_description_idrisincorporated = Idris Incorporated is an interstellar corporate bank headquartered in the Sol Alliance. The bank has begun offering hiring bonuses to those who work for other major interstellar corporations to draw people away from their competitors. However, they are still in a struggle with NanoTrasen due to its large employee base mainly using the company's bank as their method of storing funds, preventing Idris from having a large number of members.

employer_name_orionexpress = Orion Express
employer_name_orionexpress_command = Orion Express Command
employer_description_orionexpress = Orion Express is a manufactured megacorporation designed to handle logistics in the wake of the phoron scarcity, and the sudden entangling of supply lines that left the galaxy struggling for more resources. Its main branch is dedicated to cargo services and transport, but also features a fledgling robotics division mainly focused on industrial synthetics to aid in its logistics missions.

employer_name_pmcg = PMCG
employer_name_pmcg_command = PMCG Command
employer_description_pmcg = A coalition of security contractors, the Private Military Contracting Group is one of the elements born from the necessity of protecting an ever-growing corporate empire. Gathering mercenaries from all across the galaxy, the Private Military Contracting Group deploys a diverse force to anywhere they are needed.

employer_name_eastorioncompany = East-Orion Company
employer_name_eastorioncompany_command = East-Orion Company Command
employer_description_eastorioncompany = A Nederlandic initiative to exploit an untapped market in 2157, the United East-Orion Company was an old idea made new. Rooted in tradition that went back centuries, two large agricultural corporations — the New-Nederic agricultural machinery manufacturer and the Farmer's Civil Union — came together under one banner to offer planet-honed skillsets to a growing number of corporate space stations.
